    "updated_at": "2022-02-04T12:57:51Z",
    "body": "Should probably be noted that that big a bitmap is unrealistic.\r\n\r\nChrome [will throw](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/blink/renderer/core/imagebitmap/image_bitmap.cc;bpv=1;bpt=1;l=132?q=%20third_party%2Fblink%2Frenderer%2Fcore%2Fimagebitmap%2Fimage_bitmap.cc&ss=chromium%2Fchromium%2Fsrc&gsn=DstBufferSizeHasOverflow&gs=kythe%3A%2F%2Fchromium.googlesource.com%2Fchromium%2Fsrc%3Flang%3Dc%252B%252B%3Fpath%3Dsrc%2Fthird_party%2Fblink%2Frenderer%2Fcore%2Fimagebitmap%2Fimage_bitmap.cc%23joPDMincxth3v38Um-8GVtFjH3hIR_Oz_stfHcsvwxM) with an area * *bytesPerPixel* that would overflow unsigned: https://jsfiddle.net/wvhf592x\r\nSomehow Firefox allows insanely big values, but they can't draw it back anyway: https://jsfiddle.net/jq5nczed/\r\n<sub>Well they do draw something on ImageBitmapRenderingContexts but's that doesn't correspond to what was asked: https://jsfiddle.net/wvhf592x/2</sub>\r\nSafari ... does its things.\r\n\r\nSo even when IDL is fixed here, it may be good to specify that this method should throw a standardized error in such a case.",
