    "updated_at": "2022-02-07T18:44:11Z",
    "body": "Hmmm...  In the case of OOM while allocating a pixel buffer for a canvas or an ImageBitmap object, I think the only option listed in [https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#killing-scripts](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#killing-scripts) that is applicable is \"[abort the script](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#abort-a-running-script) without an exception\". I don't know of any implementations that do this.  It would be a worse UX anyways. I wonder why the common behavior of failing silently was never codified in the standard. ",
