    "created_at": "2022-02-07T20:10:09Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-02-07T20:11:17Z",
    "body": "Doesn't \"quota\" usually refer to a settable limit rather than a hardware limitation?  As far as canvas is concerned, this is moot because we have a longstanding stable interoperable behavior, which is to fail silently. That has been the de facto standard for over a decade and no one is complaining about it, so we should probably just immortalize that behavior in the standard at this point.  For createImageBitmap however, options are open because, as @Kaido found, browsers are not currently inter-operable.\r\n\r\nPersonally, I like the idea of rejecting the promise with an exception more than silent failures because it gives devs/apps feedback on the cause of the failure, and it makes the failures detectable, which allows apps to mitigate them (for example, use a lower resolution). ",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
